  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent. This brick is a pure transform of the upstream `epa-chemexpo` brick (its only dependency in .bb/dependencies.txt), which is U.S. EPA public-domain ChemExpo/CPDat data (17 U.S.C. \u00a7 105). No new data is introduced, so the class follows the parent: open / commercial permitted. The README explicitly states 'ChemExpo is U.S. EPA public-domain data'. Same caveat as the parent: ChemExpo aggregates many third-party source documents that USEPA does not review.",
